#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:492
#, no-c-format
msgid "play"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:493
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <quote>play</quote> call starts the player from where it was last stopped."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:497
#, no-c-format
msgid "playPause"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:498
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>playPause</quote> call starts the player if it is currently stopped "
"or paused. This call also pauses the player if it is currently playing a track."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:502
#, no-c-format
msgid "prev"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:503
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <quote>prev</quote> call moves the player back one track."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:507
#, no-c-format
msgid "seek"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:508
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>seek</quote> call is used to seek to a specific point in a track by "
"a value specified in seconds."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:512
#, no-c-format
msgid "seekRelative"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:513
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>seekRelative</quote> call is used to seek to a position relative to "
"the current track position by a value specified in seconds."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:517
#, no-c-format
msgid "setEqualizer"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:518
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>setEqualizer</quote> call uses eleven space delimited integers to "
"set the equalizer slider values. The slider values range from -255 as the "
"lowest value, and 255 as the highest. The first integer is used to set the "
"pre-amp value, the remaining integers set the pre-amp response frequency values "
"from 60Hz to 16kHz."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:522
#, no-c-format
msgid "setEqualizerEnabled"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:523
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>setEqualizerEnabled</quote> call is used to enable the equalizer "
"using a true or false value."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:527
#, no-c-format
msgid "setScore"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:528
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>setScore</quote> call sets the score of the current track specified "
"by a number from 0 to 100."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:532
#, no-c-format
msgid "setScoreByPath"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:533
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>setScoreByPath</quote> call sets the score of a track specified by "
"it's path followed by it's score specified by a number from 0 to 100."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:537
#, no-c-format
msgid "setVolume"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:538
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>setVolume</quote> call adjusts the volume to a level specified by a "
"value from 0 to 100."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:542
#, no-c-format
msgid "showBrowser"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:543
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>showBrowser</quote> calls shows a browser in the playlist window. "
"Valid browser values are context, collection, playlist, media and file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:547
#, no-c-format
msgid "showOSD"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:548
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>showOSD</quote> call raises the OSD to show the current track "
"information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:552
#, no-c-format
msgid "stop"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:553
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <quote>stop</quote> call will stop the player if it is currently playing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:557
#, no-c-format
msgid "volumeDown"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:558
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <quote>volumeDown</quote> call adjusts the volume down one step."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:562
#, no-c-format
msgid "volumeUp"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:563
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <quote>volumeUp</quote> call adjusts the volume up one step."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: advanced.docbook:573
#, no-c-format
msgid "dcop amarok playlist"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:587
#, no-c-format
msgid "saveCurrentPlaylist"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:588
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>saveCurrentPlaylist</quote> call saves the current playlist as "
"~/.kde/share/apps/amarok/current.xml."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:592
#, no-c-format
msgid "getActiveIndex"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:593
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>getActiveIndex</quote> call returns an integer value for the current "
"track's position in the playlist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:597
#, no-c-format
msgid "getTotalTrackCount"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:598
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>getTotalTrackCount</quote> call returns the total number of tracks "
"in the playlist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:602
#, no-c-format
msgid "addMedia"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:603
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <quote>addMedia</quote> call is used to add single files to the playlist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:607
#, no-c-format
msgid "addMediaList"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:608
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>addMediaList</quote> call is used to add multiple files to the "
"playlist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:612
#, no-c-format
msgid "clearPlaylist"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:613
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <quote>clearPlaylist</quote> call is used to clear the entire playlist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:617
#, no-c-format
msgid "playByIndex"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:618
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>playByIndex</quote> call starts playback of a track by it's position "
"in the playlist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:622
#, no-c-format
msgid "playMedia"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:623
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>playMEDIA</quote> call starts playback of a track specified by it's "
"KURL."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:627
#, no-c-format
msgid "popupMessage"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:628
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>popupMessage</quote> call starts a popup mesage in the playlist "
"window. The popup message is specified with a QString."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:632
#, no-c-format
msgid "repopulate"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:633
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>repopulate</quote> call repopulates the playlist with tracks from "
"dynamic mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:637
#, no-c-format
msgid "removeCurrentTrack"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:638
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>removeCurrentTrack</quote> call removes the current track from the "
"playlist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:642
#, no-c-format
msgid "saveM3u"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:643
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>saveM3u</quote> call saves the current playlist in the M3U format. "
"You must specify the path to save the file as, and include a value of 0 or 1 to "
"indicate whether or not to write relative paths."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:647
#, no-c-format
msgid "setStopAfterCurrent"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:648
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>setStopAfterCurrent</quote> call stops playback of the playlist "
"after the current track has completed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:652
#, no-c-format
msgid "shortStatusMessage"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:653
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>shortStatusMessage</quote> call displays a string of text as a "
"message in the status bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:657
#, no-c-format
msgid "shufflePlaylist"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:658
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>shufflePlaylist</quote> call randomizes the order of the tracks in "
"the playlist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:662
#, no-c-format
msgid "togglePlaylist"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: advanced.docbook:663
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <quote>togglePlaylist</quote> call toggles the use of the playlist window "
"either on or off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
